10	 * returned on the owner DTO; the level is also recorded on the create audit line.
11	 *
12	 * <p>Points are scored at creation, starting at {@code 0}:
13	 * <ul>
14	 *   <li>adds {@code 2} when an email address is present (non-blank);</li>
15	 *   <li>adds {@code 1} when the owner's name was unique at creation, i.e. {@code namesakeCount} is
16	 *       {@code 0} (see {@link AssignNamesakeCount});</li>
17	 *   <li>adds {@code 2} when the owner belongs to a household of 3 or more — its computed
18	 *       {@code householdId} is shared with at least two earlier owners (see
19	 *       {@link OwnerIdentity#householdIdFor}); an owner with no household — no postcode — is a
20	 *       household of one;</li>
21	 *   <li>adds {@code 3} when the owner's tenure — whole elapsed fiscal years from
22	 *       {@code registrationDate} to today (see {@link FiscalYear}) — is {@code 1} or more, i.e. at
23	 *       least one 1 July boundary has passed since registration.</li>
24	 * </ul>
25	 *
26	 * <p>The points map to a level of 1 to 4: {@code 0-1} points is level {@code 1}, {@code 2-3} is
27	 * level {@code 2}, {@code 4-5} is level {@code 3}, and {@code 6} or more is level {@code 4}. A newly
28	 * created owner has zero tenure, so a new owner scores at most {@code 5} points (2 + 1 + 2) and never
29	 * reaches level 4.
30	 *
31	 * <p>Only owners created earlier (lower id) count towards the household size, so the base points stay
32	 * fixed from creation even as the household later grows.
33	 *
34	 * <p>The banded level is then capped: an owner's level cannot exceed one above the current maximum
35	 * level among their existing household members — the earlier owners (lower id) sharing this owner's
36	 * {@code householdId}. With no existing household member (no postcode, or first in the household) no
37	 * cap applies. The cap is computed from those members' own (already-capped) levels.
38	 */
